      "link": null,
      "locked": true,
      "customData": {
        "title": "From repository to a running app",
        "description": "Read each row left to right, then continue down. Steps 1-3 configure a derived repository, approve the Entra-only identity plan, and obtain administrator consent and user sign-in. Steps 4-6 approve the untargeted platform plan, synchronize all five DEV items with Bootstrap explicitly attached, and verify local data and physical item IDs. Steps 7-9 approve the full knowledge plan, prove indexed and live retrieval, and report DEV ready only with evidence. Step 10 publishes the Foundry hosted agent and deploys the Azure Container Apps web app from the published commit, each with its own release approval, proves both as the deploying user, and ends with the user's own browser sign-in. TEST promotion, other users' access and second-user isolation remain separate.",
        "role": "page"
      },
      "index": "a0"
    },
